    {
      "id": "al11-l2",
      "title": "RAL and RAR",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "RAL (027) and RAR (037) rotate through the carry: the carry goes into the byte, and the bit that falls out goes into the carry. That's a 9-bit rotation.",
        "STC (067) sets the carry, CMC (077) flips it.",
        "Rotating through the carry links bytes together, for example to shift a 16-bit number."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "076   ; 000: MVI A",
          "200   ;      128",
          "027   ; 002: RAL",
          "323   ; 003: OUT 377",
          "377   ;      port 377",
          "027   ; 005: RAL",
          "323   ; 006: OUT 377",
          "377   ;      port 377",
          "166   ; 010: HLT"
        ],
        "output": [
          "LEDS ○○○○○○○○ = 0",
          "LEDS ○○○○○○○● = 1"
        ]
      },
      "exercises": [
