    {
      "id": "al11-l3",
      "title": "Multiply and Divide by 2",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "Shifting left doubles a number, shifting right halves it, as long as no bit falls off. Clear the carry first (ANA A does that), then RAL doubles and RAR halves.",
        "Bits that fall off the right end are the remainder: 13 halved is 6, with 1 left over.",
        "Shifting is much faster than adding in a loop, so programmers used it whenever they could."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "076   ; 000: MVI A",
          "050   ;      40",
          "247   ; 002: ANA A",
          "037   ; 003: RAR",
          "323   ; 004: OUT 377",
          "377   ;      port 377",
          "247   ; 006: ANA A",
          "037   ; 007: RAR",
          "323   ; 010: OUT 377",
          "377   ;      port 377",
          "166   ; 012: HLT"
        ],
        "output": [
          "LEDS ○○○●○●○○ = 20",
          "LEDS ○○○○●○●○ = 10"
        ]
      },
      "exercises": [
